          "solution": "```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef compute_drift_metrology(ref_arr, prod_arr, n_bins: int = 10) -> tuple[float, float, float, bool]:\n    ref = np.sort(np.asarray(ref_arr, dtype=float))\n    prod = np.sort(np.asarray(prod_arr, dtype=float))\n    all_x = np.sort(np.concatenate([ref, prod]))\n    cdf_r_all = np.searchsorted(ref, all_x, side=\"right\") / len(ref)\n    cdf_p_all = np.searchsorted(prod, all_x, side=\"right\") / len(prod)\n    D = float(np.max(np.abs(cdf_r_all - cdf_p_all)))\n    n_eff = len(ref) * len(prod) / (len(ref) + len(prod))\n    ks_p = float(min(1.0, 2.0 * np.exp(-2.0 * n_eff * D * D)))\n    deltas = np.diff(all_x)\n    w1_std = float(np.sum(np.abs(cdf_r_all[:-1] - cdf_p_all[:-1]) * deltas)) / max(float(np.std(ref)), 1e-8)\n    edges = np.quantile(ref, np.linspace(0.0, 1.0, n_bins + 1))\n    edges[0], edges[-1] = -np.inf, np.inf\n    p = np.clip(np.histogram(ref, bins=edges)[0] / len(ref), 1e-6, None)\n    q = np.clip(np.histogram(prod, bins=edges)[0] / len(prod), 1e-6, None)\n    p, q = p / p.sum(), q / q.sum()\n    psi = float(np.sum((q - p) * np.log(q / p)))\n    gate_alert = bool((w1_std > 0.25) or (psi > 0.20))\n    return (round(ks_p, 6), round(w1_std, 4), round(psi, 4), gate_alert)\n```"
